{"abstract":[{"text":"How a client proves its identity at the token endpoint (RFC 8705 §2, OIDC Core §9 naming).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Only the methods AXIAM actually implements are representable. ","type":"text"},{"code":"None","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the public-client","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value — was deliberately absent until T21.2: adding it before the rest of the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"understood one would have let an operator register a client whose authentication is silently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped. The server understands one now (","type":"text"},{"code":"token.rs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"authenticate_client_credential","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an arm that accepts ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" credential and refuses a presented one, the authorization endpoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derives its PKCE requirement from this enum, and the admin API refuses the method alongside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any grant or binding that contradicts it), so the variant exists — and only that arm may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ever treat a missing credential as success.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SH","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SY","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientauthmethod"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClientAuthMethod"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"open"}]},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"access. ","type":"text"},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is never written: ","type":"text"},{"code":"encode(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" refuses it locally, before any request, as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validation failure (CONTRACT.md §34.2 P12.2, contract 1.60 A4) — never as ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the server to refuse. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over these cases needs an ","type":"text"},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arm.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/clientSecretBasic","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/clientSecretPost","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/none","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/privateKeyJWT","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/selfSignedTLSClientAuth","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/tlsClientAuth","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/unknown"],"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/init(from:)-4qajg","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/init(rawValue:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/encode(to:)"],"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/RawRepresentable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK16ClientAuthMethodO","symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClientAuthMethod","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"title":"ClientAuthMethod","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ClientAuthMethod","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/SQ":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientAuthMethod"